{"records":[{"id":"f7btcr6x6d","title":"A non-canonical function of glutathione to suppress ferroptosis via FSP1","description":"Whole genome-wide CRISPR KO screen","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-10-02T11:41:52.925Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/f7btcr6x6d","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/f7btcr6x6d"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"BO","last_name":"CHU","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"nxvdzybwhf","title":"Illuminating host-mycobacterial interactions with genome-wide CRISPR knockout and CRISPRi screens","description":"The data deposited here contains genome-wide CRISPR knockout and CRISPRi screen data, including the positive hits, the negative hits, and non-targeting controls. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-08-30T11:32:01.108Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/nxvdzybwhf","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/nxvdzybwhf"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yong","last_name":"Lai","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Functional Genomics","High-Throughput Sequencing","Tuberculosis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"s3jtdhjdbs","title":"Supplementary data for Michaelis et al., 'Protein import motor complex reacts to mitochondrial misfolding by reducing protein import and activating mitophagy'","description":"Supplementary data for Michaelis et al., 'Mitochondrial import loss induces mitophagy without membrane depolarization'. We hypothesized that inhibition of mitochondrial protein import induced mitophagy independent of mitochondrial depolarization. This dataset contains raw Illumina sequencing data for all samples from a genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 screen for mitophagy regulators. The genome-wide library is Brunello from Doench et al Nat Biotechnol. 2016. We found that the pre-sequence translocase-associated motor complex PAM controls mitophagy induction. Loss of PAM caused a loss in protein import and was sufficient to induce mitophagy without depolarization.\nThe samples have been sequenced on an Illumina NextSeq 500 in single end mode with 75+8 cycles. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-08-05T15:38:53.752Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/s3jtdhjdbs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/s3jtdhjdbs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jonas","last_name":"Michaelis","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Melinda","last_name":"Brunstein","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Süleyman","last_name":"Bozkurt","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ludovico","last_name":"Alves","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Martin","last_name":"Wegner","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Manuel","last_name":"Kaulich","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Christian","last_name":"Pohl","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Christian","last_name":"Münch","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Proteomics","Mitochondrion","Mitophagy","Genetic Screening","Next Generation Sequencing","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"65pfcj4j4m","title":"Protocol of CRISPR-Cas9 knockout screens for identifying ferroptosis regulators","description":"Ferroptosis, an iron-dependent programmed cell death triggered by excessive lipid peroxidation, has shown promising therapeutic potentials in human diseases. Here, we describe a protocol of a CRISPR-Cas9 loss-of-function screen to identify regulators in response to different inducers of ferroptosis. We emphasize the steps of library amplification, drug treatment, high-throughput sequencing preparation, and bioinformatics analysis using Model-based Analysis of Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 Knockout (MAGeCK). We also present a method to discover the regulators of ferroptosis and verify the potential targets efficiently.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-10-24T01:46:48.793Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/65pfcj4j4m","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/65pfcj4j4m"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Yang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wei","last_name":"Gu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR/Cas9","Ferroptosis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"nnxh5d35nd","title":"Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 screen identified KLF11 as a druggable suppressor for sarcoma cancer stem cells","description":"The original, unprocessed data alongside the paper","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-05-31T01:39:45.722Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/nnxh5d35nd","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/nnxh5d35nd"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Le","last_name":"Qu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"8xhv88c7wt","title":"Genome-wide screening in human kidney organoids identifies developmental and disease-related aspects of nephrogenesis","description":"Human organoids allow the study of proliferation, lineage specification, and three-dimensional tissue development. Here, we present a genome-wide CRISPR screen in iPSC-derived kidney organoids. The combination of inducible genome editing, longitudinal sampling and endpoint sorting of tubular and stromal cells generated a complex, high-quality dataset uncovering a broad spectrum of insightful biology from early development to ‘adult’ epithelial morphogenesis. Our functional dataset allows improving mesoderm induction by ROCK inhibition, contains monogenetic and complex trait kidney disease genes, confirms two additional CAKUT genes (CCDC170 and MYH7B), and provides a large candidate list of ciliopathy-related genes. Finally, the identification of a cis-inhibitory effect of Jagged1 controlling epithelial proliferation shows how mosaic knockouts in pooled CRISPR screening can discover ways of communication between heterogeneous cell populations in complex tissues. Collectively, these data serve both as a rich resource for the kidney community and as a benchmark for future iPSC-derived organoid CRISPR screens.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-11-29T13:48:59.335Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/8xhv88c7wt","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/8xhv88c7wt"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Rosemarie","last_name":"Ungricht","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Philipp","last_name":"Hoppe","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Screening","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"zhpg8xshp9","title":"Lawrence et al., PNAS 2026","description":"Data from “Lawrence et al., 2026 A Genome-Wide Screen Identifies that PLCG2 Restrains Lysosomal GCase Activity.\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-06-22T18:23:16.389Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/zhpg8xshp9","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/zhpg8xshp9"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Baris","last_name":"Bingol","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Natural Sciences"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"xn3vv2cdnk","title":"High-throughput CRISPR screens to dissect macrophage-Shigella interactions","description":"The positive hits, negative hits, and non-targeting controls of genome-wide CRISPR screens; Supplemental Tables.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-07-23T06:18:30.182Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xn3vv2cdnk","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xn3vv2cdnk"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yong","last_name":"LAI","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Genetic Screening","Host-Pathogen Interaction","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"y8dndzn3mg","title":"Genome-scale CRISPR screen identifies TMEM41B as a critical host factor required for coronavirus replication","description":"These data are part of the Supplemental Items associated with the manuscript entitled \"Genome-scale CRISPR screen identifies TMEM41B as a critical host factor required for coronavirus replication\". These files include Supplementary Data file 1-4.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-03-16T10:34:13.579Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/y8dndzn3mg","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/y8dndzn3mg"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Limeng","last_name":"Sun","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Virus","Screening","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"66ms37y66x","title":"Data for: A genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 screen reveals that riboflavin regulates hydrogen peroxide entry into HAP1 cells  ","description":"CRISPR screen data for hydrogen peroxide mediated cell death","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-02-13T14:30:16.414Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/66ms37y66x","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/66ms37y66x"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"surachai","last_name":"supattapone","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kenneth","last_name":"Mark","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Tamutenda","last_name":"Chidawanyika","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Oxidative Stress"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":119805,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":155,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":119805,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":119265,"restricted":61,"embargoed":479},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2043},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":602},{"id":"https://ror